---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software distributed with Vestra
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT terms above cover Vestra's own source code. Packaged builds also carry
programs under their own licences, which are unaffected by the above.

mpv (https://mpv.io) — GPL-2.0-or-later
    Packaged builds include an mpv executable, used to decode and render video.
    mpv is a separate program: Vestra starts it as its own process and speaks
    to it over a local socket. It is not linked into Vestra, and the two remain
    separate works.

    Vestra does not modify mpv. The exact upstream release shipped is recorded
    in `resources/mpv/mpv-build.json` beside the binary, alongside a NOTICE
    naming the corresponding sources:

        https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv
        https://github.com/shinchiro/mpv-winbuild-cmake

    The full GPL text is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html

Electron, Chromium and their dependencies
    Distributed under their respective licences. Packaged builds include
    `LICENSES.chromium.html` with the complete text.

Skip timings are retrieved at runtime from AniSkip (https://aniskip.com) and
are not distributed with Vestra.
